---
# The WireGuard private key, as a FILE rather than an env var (2026-07-15 review L2): inlined as
# MULLVAD_PRIVATE_KEY it would land in the container's environment, which anything able to
# read the pod spec can see. The LSIO base's init-envfile reads FILE__<VAR> from the file into
# <VAR> before the mullvad mod runs. The account number has a Secret of its own,
# qbittorrent-mullvad-account (mullvad-account-secret.yaml.j2), because its all-digit value
# cannot pass through a Flux placeholder. The Deployment projects both Secrets into one volume.
#
# The key renders as stored, with no transform, so stored surrounding whitespace reaches the
# Secret unchanged. init-envfile does NOT strip a trailing newline (it only warns), and a
# newline corrupts the key. Nothing at deploy strips or refuses one: store the value without
# surrounding whitespace.
#
# Rendered through manifests_secret_files, so the file on disk is 0600 and the task carries
# no_log.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: qbittorrent-mullvad
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  key: "{{ wireguard_interface_private_key }}"
